      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5baf2b2de038c00e28fd16b5|full_name}: From what I can gather, objects that are not related to the avatar (like sword models, hat models, etc.) that constraints to the avatar's armature (rotation and position), like you said, \"kind of works\". It'll jitter, and have a slight delay with tracking the constraint object. (A hand for example)\nFor one of my avatars, I have an xmas gift object on the right hand, with a lid that I can pull with the left hand via constraints.\nJitters and inaccuracy for the lid REALLY show in the mirror when I move my right arm super fast while holding the lid on the left hand.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
